From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 09:56:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: read and set the backlight without nvkms_lock

The backlight class callbacks took the global nvkms_lock around
nvKmsSetBacklight() / nvKmsGetBacklight(), which only make one RM control
call (NV0073 SET/GET_BACKLIGHT_BRIGHTNESS, a GSP RPC of 0.1-2.7 ms) on the
display's RM objects and touch no NVKMS state. Every brightness read or
change from userspace therefore stalled NVKMS ioctls, vblank callbacks and
flip completion events for the duration of the RPC.

The lock isn't needed for lifetime either: the backlight core calls these
callbacks with bd->ops_lock held, and nvkms_unregister_backlight() (called
from nvFreeCoreChannelEvo() before the display RM objects are freed) takes
ops_lock in backlight_device_unregister(). Taking nvkms_lock in the
callbacks could in fact deadlock against that unregistration, which runs
with nvkms_lock held while a callback holding ops_lock waits for nvkms_lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c     | 29 +++++++------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
index 09967590..c8558efe 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-modeset/nvidia-modeset-linux.c
@@ -1298,19 +1298,20 @@ static int nvkms_update_backlight_status(struct backlight_device *bd)
 {
     struct nvkms_backlight_device *nvkms_bd = bl_get_data(bd);
     NvBool status;
-    int ret;
-
-    ret = down_interruptible(&nvkms_lock);
-
-    if (ret != 0) {
-        return ret;
-    }
 
+    /*
+     * nvKmsSetBacklight() and nvKmsGetBacklight() only make an RM control
+     * call on the display's RM objects and don't touch NVKMS state, so they
+     * run without nvkms_lock (the RM call is a GSP RPC that can take
+     * milliseconds). The backlight core calls them with
+     * bd->ops_lock held, and nvkms_unregister_backlight() takes ops_lock
+     * before NVKMS frees the display, which keeps drv_priv valid here.
+     * Taking nvkms_lock here can also deadlock against
+     * nvkms_unregister_backlight(), which runs with nvkms_lock held.
+     */
     status = nvKmsSetBacklight(nvkms_bd->display_id, nvkms_bd->drv_priv,
                                bd->props.brightness);
 
-    up(&nvkms_lock);
-
     return status ? 0 : -EINVAL;
 }
 
@@ -1319,19 +1320,11 @@ static int nvkms_get_backlight_brightness(struct backlight_device *bd)
     struct nvkms_backlight_device *nvkms_bd = bl_get_data(bd);
     NvU32 brightness = 0;
     NvBool status;
-    int ret;
-
-    ret = down_interruptible(&nvkms_lock);
-
-    if (ret != 0) {
-        return ret;
-    }
 
+    /* No nvkms_lock, see nvkms_update_backlight_status(). */
     status = nvKmsGetBacklight(nvkms_bd->display_id, nvkms_bd->drv_priv,
                                &brightness);
 
-    up(&nvkms_lock);
-
     return  status ? brightness : -1;
 }
 
